WEBVTT

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.389 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>ALBUM — Asset Localization By Unified Matching</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.790 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>ALBUM takes unposed RGB views,</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:09.842 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>point prompts, and a user-supplied asset library.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.111 --> 00:00:13.101 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>In one forward pass, ALBUM retrieves each asset</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.101 --> 00:00:15.700 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>and predicts its 7DoF layout.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.520 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>How does a point become a placed asset?</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.671 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>Here, it selects the coffee table in front of the sofa.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.585 --> 00:00:25.275 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>The encoder combines SAM appearance features</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:27.785 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>with geometry from Depth Anything 3.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.785 --> 00:00:31.289 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>It gathers evidence across views into instance tokens.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:36.500 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>DINOv3 encodes canonical views of the library assets.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.020 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>A shared matcher compares each candidate</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.557 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>with the table’s instance tokens and selects the best match.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.502 --> 00:00:46.292 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>The layout decoder uses those same tokens,</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.292 --> 00:00:49.762 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>along with the asset’s surface positions and viewing directions,</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.762 --> 00:00:53.652 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>to predict translation, rotation, and uniform scale</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.652 --> 00:00:54.792 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>in the first camera’s frame.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.335 --> 00:00:58.305 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>We retain DA3’s camera pose and depth predictions</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.305 --> 00:01:01.003 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>to place the table back in the reconstructed room.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.543 --> 00:01:03.543 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>If the exact object is missing,</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.543 --> 00:01:06.053 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>you can supply our library or your own.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.053 --> 00:01:08.863 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>ALBUM retrieves the highest-scoring substitute</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.863 --> 00:01:10.333 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>and estimates its layout.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.543 --> 00:01:17.353 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>The retrieved mesh keeps its original materials,</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.353 --> 00:01:19.685 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>even on surfaces hidden from the cameras.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.043 --> 00:01:23.963 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>On Replica, both the rooms and their asset libraries</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.963 --> 00:01:25.733 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>were unseen during training.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.733 --> 00:01:27.507 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>The network weights stay fixed.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.043 --> 00:01:32.593 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>Source assets keep their articulation joints,</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.593 --> 00:01:35.462 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>so drawers slide and cabinet doors swing open.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.543 --> 00:01:39.233 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>The meshes are editable, too.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:42.535 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>We rigged this wardrobe door to slide across the other panel.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.043 --> 00:01:48.173 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>ALBUM places several objects in one forward pass.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.173 --> 00:01:50.413 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>Their point prompts share scene features,</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.413 --> 00:01:52.937 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>and their layouts use the same camera frame.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.043 --> 00:01:56.733 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>We collected over 2,000 3D assets</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.733 --> 00:01:58.715 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>created by artists and designers.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.055 --> 00:02:04.255 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>The full ALBUM library contains 6,961 textured assets</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.255 --> 00:02:06.138 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>across 97 categories.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.478 --> 00:02:09.658 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>Of these, 4,236 are static</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.658 --> 00:02:12.835 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>and 2,725 are articulated.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.585 --> 00:02:16.885 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>We furnished 100,414 layouts,</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.885 --> 00:02:18.925 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>placing supporting furniture first</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.925 --> 00:02:21.798 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>and checking for collisions as other objects are added.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.585 --> 00:02:26.835 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>Multiple views link each instance mask</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.835 --> 00:02:29.395 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>to its source asset and 3D layout,</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.395 --> 00:02:31.796 line:-1 position:50% size:94% align:center
&nbsp;&nbsp;<c.words>supervising both matching and placement.</c>&nbsp;&nbsp;
